### WalletFlow API examples (VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP client)
@host = http://localhost:8080
@v = api/v1

### Register a customer
POST {{host}}/{{v}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@example.test", "password": "CorrectHorse123" }

### Login -> copy accessToken / refreshToken into the variables below
POST {{host}}/{{v}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@example.test", "password": "CorrectHorse123" }

@token = <paste accessToken>
@refresh = <paste refreshToken>

### Rotate the refresh token (the old one stops working)
POST {{host}}/{{v}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refresh}}" }

### Open a wallet
POST {{host}}/{{v}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "currency": "TRY" }

@account = <paste account id>
@other = <paste another account id>

### Top up through the payment provider (retry-safe thanks to Idempotency-Key)
POST {{host}}/{{v}}/accounts/{{account}}/topups
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: topup-0001-abcdef
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 250.00, "sourceToken": "tok_visa" }

### Simulate a declined card -> 402 problem+json, balance unchanged
POST {{host}}/{{v}}/accounts/{{account}}/topups
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: topup-0002-abcdef
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 10.00, "sourceToken": "tok_declined" }

### Transfer. Send it twice: the second call replays the first response, money moves once.
POST {{host}}/{{v}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: transfer-0001-abcdef
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fromAccountId": "{{account}}", "toAccountId": "{{other}}", "amount": 40.50, "reference": "rent" }

### Same key, different amount -> 422 idempotency.key_reused
POST {{host}}/{{v}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Idempotency-Key: transfer-0001-abcdef
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fromAccountId": "{{account}}", "toAccountId": "{{other}}", "amount": 99.00, "reference": "rent" }

### Transaction history (paged)
GET {{host}}/{{v}}/accounts/{{account}}/transactions?page=1&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Admin: freeze an account (needs an Admin token)
PATCH {{host}}/{{v}}/admin/accounts/{{account}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Frozen" }

### Admin/Auditor: audit trail
GET {{host}}/{{v}}/admin/audit-logs?page=1&size=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
